 "verdict": "THE REGISTERED READOUT IS NOT A READOUT, SO THE MECHANISM IS UNTESTED: 'bodies besides the pair at the sample of minimum count' comes out at 1 exactly when the pair fused and 0 exactly when it did not - in 24 of 24 runs, because the merged body drifts more than three cells from the seeded centres and is then counted as a body besides the pair, while an unfused pair sits inside that radius and counts as none. With one component on the field there is nothing besides it, so the quantity is the outcome restated and cannot speak about nucleation; its two levels differ by +0 at radius 6, which is that identity rather than a measurement. What the experiment DOES establish is that X186's sign flip reproduces under a designed manipulation of one variable: the colder body's inflow moves the share +0.67 at radius 3 (0 of 6 cold against 4 of 6 warm - the law's direction) and -0.33 at radius 6 (6 of 6 cold against 4 of 6 warm - the flipped direction), so the flip is not a per-cell selection artefact of X186; its mechanism is still open and the registered readout cannot find it. The plan's third branch ('nucleation is general') is not taken either: at radius 3 the warm level 'shows more extra bodies' only because the cold level never reached one component, which is the same degeneracy."
}
